---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Download the data | Aether Flight"
	description="Every table behind the explorer as Parquet: the FAA registry joined to adsb.lol's open ADS-B archive, school fleets, and the findings. ODbL.">
	<Header />
	<main class="data">
		<h1>Take it home</h1>
		<p class="lede">Every table behind the explorer, as Parquet you can query straight from the URL. No account, no API key.</p>

		<section>
			<h2>Try it</h2>
			<p>With <a href="https://duckdb.org/docs/installation/">DuckDB</a> installed, this asks how many registered gyroplanes actually flew:</p>
			<pre><code id="try">duckdb -c "SELECT count(*) AS registered,
  count(*) FILTER (WHERE observed_class &lt;&gt; 'not_observed') AS heard
FROM 'https://data.aether-flight.com/v/RELEASE/aircraft.parquet'
WHERE aircraft_type = 'Gyroplane'"</code></pre>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>Files</h2>
			<p id="meta" class="dim">Loading the current release…</p>
			<ul id="files" class="files"></ul>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>What's in each table</h2>
			<dl>
				<dt><code>aircraft.parquet</code></dt><dd>One row per N-number on the FAA registry snapshot: registration fields, and what adsb.lol observed in the window (days, hours, legs, first and last seen, home airport, LADD flag).</dd>
				<dt><code>aircraft_day/YYYY-MM.parquet</code></dt><dd>One row per aircraft per day: points by source, observed airborne minutes, legs, callsigns, last ground position.</dd>
				<dt><code>legs/YYYY-MM.parquet</code></dt><dd>One row per observed leg: start and end time and position, departure and arrival airport when the aircraft was seen low near one.</dd>
				<dt><code>schools.json</code></dt><dd>Flight schools and clubs: fleets and rates from each school's own website (with the source page), FAA registry matches, and observed activity.</dd>
				<dt><code>unmatched.parquet</code></dt><dd>US-block addresses heard on ADS-B that are not on the registry snapshot. Not an estimate of privacy-address use.</dd>
				<dt><code>results.json</code>, <code>training.json</code>, <code>privacy.json</code></dt><dd>The frozen numbers behind the findings, with definitions and window.</dd>
			</dl>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>License</h2>
			<p>Contains information from <a href="https://github.com/adsblol/globe_history_2026">adsb.lol</a>, which is made available here under the
				<a href="https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/">Open Database License (ODbL)</a>. These tables are released under the ODbL too:
				use them for anything, including commercially; if you publish a database built from them, share it under the ODbL. FAA registry data is
				public domain. Nothing here is derived from OpenSky or AOPA data, whose terms forbid redistribution. Each release includes a
				<code>LICENSES.md</code> with the provenance of every file.</p>
		</section>
	</main>
	<Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<script>
	const base = 'https://data.aether-flight.com';
	const mb = (b: number) => (b >= 1e6 ? `${(b / 1e6).toFixed(0)} MB` : `${Math.max(1, Math.round(b / 1e3))} KB`);
	(async () => {
		const meta = document.getElementById('meta')!;
		try {
			const { release } = await fetch(`${base}/latest.json`, { cache: 'no-store' }).then((r) => r.json());
			const m = await fetch(`${base}/v/${release}/manifest.json`).then((r) => r.json());
			meta.textContent = `Release ${release} · window ${m.window.first_day} → ${m.window.last_day} (${m.window.days} days)`;
			document.getElementById('files')!.innerHTML = m.files
				.map((f: any) => `<li><a href="${base}/v/${release}/${f.path}">${f.path}</a><span>${mb(f.bytes)}</span></li>`).join('');
			const code = document.getElementById('try')!;
			code.textContent = code.textContent!.replace('RELEASE', release);
		} catch (e: any) {
			meta.textContent = `The download index did not load (${e.message}). Files are at ${base}/latest.json.`;
		}
	})();
</script>

<style>
	.data { position: relative; z-index: 1; max-width: 72ch; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1rem 4rem; }
	h1 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 400; font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 7vw, 3.2rem); color: var(--text-bright); margin: 1rem 0 .5rem; }
	h2 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 400; font-size: 1.4rem; color: var(--text-bright); margin: 2.25rem 0 .75rem; }
	.lede, .dim { color: var(--text-dim); }
	p { font-size: .85rem; }
	pre { background: var(--strip-paper); color: var(--strip-ink); padding: .9rem 1rem; overflow-x: auto; font-size: .75rem; margin-top: .75rem; border-left: 10px solid var(--edge-active); }
	.files { list-style: none; margin-top: .5rem; }
	.files li { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; padding: .4rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); font-size: .8rem; }
	.files span { color: var(--text-dim); white-space: nowrap; }
	dl { display: grid; gap: .3rem 1rem; font-size: .8rem; }
	dt { color: var(--text-bright); margin-top: .6rem; }
	dd { color: var(--text-dim); }
	a { color: var(--chart-highlight); }
</style>
